module.exports = "A completed lesson tells you that a learner reached the end of the material. It does not tell you whether they did anything with it.\n\nFor a course owner, three questions are more useful: What did the learner do? What did they produce? Who reviewed it?\n\nIn the Seturon product model, we track three signals separately:\n\n• lesson_completed — the learner completed the lesson\n• assignment_submitted — the learner submitted the result of an action\n• assignment_reviewed — an instructor reviewed and graded the work\n\nThese are separate checkpoints in one learning workflow.\n\nIn the current specification, assignment submission is linked to the Submit action, while assignment review is linked to instructor grading. The implementation tests cover the persisted states pending → underReview → reviewed, including the grade and review comment.\n\nThis is implementation evidence from the specification and tests. It does not, by itself, demonstrate deployed usage or learner outcomes.\n\nThe checkpoints describe a learning loop that can be observed and reviewed:\n\nlesson → action → observable output → review.\n\nTake one lesson from your course and check:\n\n• What action should the learner perform?\n• What output can someone observe or assess?\n• Where does feedback or evaluation happen?\n\nIf any of these questions has no clear answer, lesson completion alone does not show that the learning work took place.";
